<title>USA: Northrop Grumman sees $12 bln sales by 2001.</title>
<headline>Northrop Grumman sees $12 bln sales by 2001.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northrop Grumman Corp expects annual sales of $12 billion by 2001, Kent Kresa, the company's chairman, president and chief executive, said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The company previously forecast sales of $10 billion by the end of the 1990s, a spokesman said.</p>
<p>At the company's annual meeting, Kresa said the new forecast was based on the company's current program base and its proposed merger with Logicon Inc, a defense information technology company.</p>
<p>For 1996, Northrop Grumman reported sales of $8.1 billion and earnings of $234 million.</p>
<p>Northrop Grumman shares were 7/8 higher at 85 late Wednesday afternoon.</p>
